{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q137110710","formula":"C₁₃H₂₁NO₂","hill":"C13H21NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":21.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Florence"},"descriptions":{"en":"Florence, also known as 2-ethoxy-5-methoxy-4-methylamphetamine or as DOM-2ETO, is a chemical compound of the phenethylamine, amphetamine, and DOx families related to DOM. It is the derivative of DOM in which the methoxy group at the 2 position has been replaced with an ethoxy group analogously to in the TWEETIO series. According to Alexander Shulgin in his book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved), Florence may have been synthesized but is not known to have been tested. Along with its positional isomer Iris (DOM-5ETO), the compound is one of Shulgin's \"ten classic ladies\", a series of methylated DOM derivatives."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOc1cc(C)c(OC)cc1CC(C)N","inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":null,"atoms":37,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.843,"y":4.124,"z":-0.396,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.182,"y":2.83,"z":-1.113,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.156,"y":1.733,"z":-0.202,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.016,"y":0.98,"z":-0.102,"el":"C"},{"x":1.239,"y":1.361,"z":-0.583,"el":"C"},{"x":2.357,"y":0.52,"z":-0.44,"el":"C"},{"x":3.693,"y":0.958,"z":-0.975,"el":"C"},{"x":2.214,"y":-0.725,"z":0.192,"el":"C"},{"x":3.351,"y":-1.486,"z":0.275,"el":"O"},{"x":3.212,"y":-2.804,"z":0.789,"el":"C"},{"x":0.964,"y":-1.098,"z":0.692,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.152,"y":-0.251,"z":0.562,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.489,"y":-0.701,"z":1.118,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.38,"y":-1.393,"z":0.065,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.837,"y":-1.412,"z":0.53,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.941,"y":-2.775,"z":-0.183,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.923,"y":4.976,"z":-1.077,"el":"H"},{"x"